e Research with Impact Dissertations Discover the research Collaboration Open sub-navigation Developing Expertise For Companies and Organisations Innovations and Technology Transfer International Collaboration Strategic Partnerships University Open sub-navigation Organisation and management Information on University Come Work with Us Strategy Quality Management Logo, Photos and Brochure of the University of Turku Faculties Faculty of Education Faculty of Humanities Faculty of Law Faculty of Medicine Faculty of Science Faculty of Social Sciences Faculty of Technology Turku School of Economics Independent Units Centre for Language and Communication Studies Turku PET Centre Finnish Centre for Astronomy with ESO Turku Bioscience Centre News Open sub-navigation For Media News and Press Releases Events Podcasts Aurora online magazine Library For Students For Media For Visitors For Alumni Breadcrumb Home University Come work with us! Open Vacancies at the University of Turku Instructions for submitting a job application via the eRekry System Here you can find instructions how to use the recruitment system and answers to frequently asked questions. I am a new job applicant You don’t need specified registration to eRekry-system. Applying to an open vacancy is done by filling in an application and attaching the required documents in the system. The link to the application form is at the top and at the end of the job advertisement (Apply for this position) . After that you can start filling information to the form. Depending on the nature of the job, fill in the following tabs: Basic information Education Language skills Work experience Other information (depending on the position) Additional information Attachments The data fields marked with a star* are mandatory. Fill in the basic information carefully. You can send the application unfinished and return to it later (Send application) . However, all fields marked with *the asterisk must be filled first. Fill in your personal email address, as all the emails from the recruitment system and the University are sent to this address. On the Education and language skills tab, fill in your degree information. We recommend that all the education and degree information that are relevant to the job should be filled in in the system. You can have more fields by clicking dark ball with white line inside. On the language skills, mandatory fields are information of Finnish and English language skills. You should also include all your relevant work experience . You can add max. three positions / employers by choosing Add new . Guestions Do you have experience of management (staff) responsibility and Do you have experience of financial responsibility are related to past activities in positions of responsibility. If you say Yes to the question of financial responsibility, you should also give an assessment of the extent of financial responsibility. We can send feedback of your application if you have chosen “I'm open to receiving feedback on my application” section. When the application is completed, click Send application . The system informs that your application was saved successfully. Logging in to the recruitment system You can log in to the system here: erekry.utu.fi/en View our open positions: www.utu.fi/careers I have not received a confirmation message regarding the submission of an application. Why? Please first double-check that you have submitted the application by clicking Send application . The system informs that your application was saved successfully. Please check also, that your email-address in your application is right. Can I change the language of the system? The system can be used in Finnish and in English. Choose the language from the language menu which is on the bottom right side of the window. Please check your browser’s language settings if you cannot access the recruitment system in the language of your choice. Video questions The application form may contain questions that are answered in a video. The video questions can always be found at the end of the application form. Before taping your video answer, please check that you have added your email address to the email field at the beginning of the application form (mandatory field). Also check that you have accepted the privacy policy , which can be found above the video window. After this, you can record your answer video. You can record the video as many times as you want. The new recording is always saved over the old recording. After sending the application you can not modify your video answers. How can I ensure that the information I entered has been saved? When the application is completed, click Send application . The system informs that your application was saved successfully. You can edit your application via the link sent to your email. Can I continue to complete my application later or cancel my application? You have 6 hours to complete your application before the timeout. You can edit your application via the link sent to your email. If the link doesn’t open straight from email, please copy the link to browser. The application can be edited until the end of the application period. If there are questions in the application form that are answered with a video, these questions cannot be edited after the application has been submitted. So please make sure that you are happy with you video answers before sending the application. You can also cancel your application via the link by choosing Withdraw from the process. At what time do application processes end? Application processes end on the date indicated in the job ad and at time mentioned in job ad, local Helsinki time (EEST). Please notice, that the end time of ad can vary. Supported browsers and file formats We recommend that you use Mozilla Firefox, Edge or Google Chrome as your browser. Cookies and pop-ups must be enabled in your browser settings. The allowed file formats are: .png, .jpg, .jpeg, .pdf, .txt, .doc, .docx, .zip, .odt, .odp, .mp3, .pptx. Note that publications can be attached only in a compressed .zip format. You can include several document files in the compressed .zip file. You can delete the Attachment by choosing X in the end of the Attachment. Attachments Attach the requested documents in the Attachments tab . You can only add one document to each requested attachment. The allowed file formats are: .png, .jpg, .jpeg, .pdf, .txt, .doc, .docx, .zip, .odt, .odp, .mp3, .pptx. Note that publications can be attached only in a compressed .zip format. You can include several document files in the compressed .zip file. You can delete the Attachment by choosing X in the end of the Attachment. The maximum sizes of the attachments are as follows: pdf, word >10 MB per attachment portfolio 25 MB images 25 MB zip-packages 80 MB (selected publications) If needed, the PDF files can be optimized through this link. Further information If you have any question about the recruitment system, please contact eRekry@utu.fi If you have any questions about the open vacancies or application, contact the person or email address provided in the job advertisement. University of Turku as an employer Open vacancies at Turku University Researcher Career Teaching Portfolio University of Turku FI-20014 Turun yliopisto, Finland Phone number: +358 29 450 5000 People Search Contact Information & Invoicing Address Campus Map HR Excellence in Research Privacy Notice Description of Document Publicity & Information Requests Whistleblowing Accessibility Statement Feedback Intranet & Online Tools Cookie Settings Main navigation at footer Home Study at UTU Research Collaboration University News Icon/Icon-fb Created with Sketch. University of Turku on Facebook Logo University of Turku on Instagram Icon-Bluesky University of Turku on Bsky Icon/Icon-youtube Created with Sketch. University of Turku on Youtube Icon/Icon-linkedin Created with Sketch. University of Turku on Linkedin Icon/Icon-TikTok Created by JV University of Turku on Tiktok Scroll to top Top Icon/Icon-fb Created with Sketch. Layer 1 Logo Icon/Icon-linkedin Created with Sketch. Layer 1 Icon/Icon-twitter Created with Sketch. Icon/Icon-TikTok Created by JV Icon/Icon-youtube Created with Sketch. Icon-Bluesky"
